If someone has a nosebleed, first assess if there's a head or spinal injury; if not, have them sit with their head slightly forward. Gently pinch the soft part of their nose, maintaining pressure for about 10 minutes until bleeding stops. Advise them not to blow their nose for a few hours to prevent another bleed.
