[2026-09-30T20:54:40.719Z] INFO faser.utils_med: As a lone rescuer performing chest compressions on an infant, encircle the infant's chest and use two fingers to give 30 compressions just below the nipple line at a rate of 100-120 per minute, to a depth of about 1.5 inches (4 cm) or one-third of the chest depth. Ensure minimal interruptions to maintain a consistent rhythm. After completing the compressions, give 2 breaths, and repeat the cycle of 30 compressions to 2 breaths until help arrives. If rescue breaths are ineffective, continue with the compressions only and call for emergency services if feasible.
