2. Place your mouth over the victim’s mouth AND NOSE to create a tight seal.  
3. Blow into the infant’s nose and mouth over 1 second, with just enough volume and force 
to cause the chest to rise with each breath. Be careful not to ventilate too  forcefully, as 
doing so may cause lung damage.  
4. If the chest does not rise, repeat the head tilt -chin lift and try to ventilate the victim again. 
